

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 7

                                  FOR

                                 CIRCE







          Marco Calabresi
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  German philosopher George Hegel, 1821:
  "In England even the poorest of people believe they have Rights; this is 
very different from what satisfies the poor in other lands."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  Winter gave way to fragrant spring.  Circe disbanded the 26th Were-Beasts.
  Balmwood was magically flooded.
  An army coming from the empire of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) 
invaded Khalturin, hoping to conquer that province owned by Circe and made 
up of extensive Plains.  Khalturin was conquered and occupied by Alain (#33)
's host.  Alain leads approximately 1 Phalanx, 1 Legion, 3 Dragons and 2 
Trolls.
  With the advent of the early summer season Circe journeyed to Chirfa.

  A host of warriors carried the banner of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
(#0) into the Mountain province of Moongard, ruled by Circe.  Tlazolteotl 
(#88)'s forces took Moongard without any major battles.  Tlazolteotl leads 
approximately 2 Phalanx and 3 Dragons.
  Midsummer's day came and went and a pleasant late summer arrived.  Circe 
journeyed to Chaco.

  Ships bearing the battle-standards of the Babba Sissoko (#0)ian empire 
cruised into the Sea province of Donegal, a land defended by the soldiers of 
Circe.  Alain (#33)'s forces conquered Donegal without any major 
engagements.  Alain leads approximately 1 Phalanx, 1 Legion, 4 Dragons and 2 
Trolls.

  Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0)'s minions initiated a campaign of 
conquest in Kaluga, a Plain province owing allegiance to Circe.  Migfox 
(#65)'s armies took possession of Kaluga practically uncontested.  Migfox 
leads approximately 2 Light Cavalry.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) invaded the province of Trouthome, a 
Desert area owned by Circe.  Tlazolteotl (#88)'s forces experienced little 
resistance in Trouthome and Tlazolteotl there established our rule.  
Tlazolteotl leads approximately 4 Phalanx and 3 Dragons.

  A fleet owing their allegiance to Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) 
invaded the province of the Constitution Sea, a Sea area ruled by Circe.  
The Constitution Sea was overrun by Bagmore (#75)'s fleet.  Bagmore leads 
approximately 1 Eagles.
  The summer surrendered to fall.  Circe travelled to Trouthome.

  A great host of warriors carried the banner of 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) into the Desert province of Kerry, 
ruled by Circe.  Rainulf (#25)'s forces experienced little opposition in 
Kerry and Rainulf there established our rule.

  A fleet sent by the empire of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) 
invaded the Terran Sea, hoping to conquer that province ruled by Circe and 
made up of extensive Seas.  Bagmore (#75)'s forces encountered little 
opposition in the Terran Sea and Bagmore there established our rule.  
Bagmore leads approximately 1 Eagles.
  With the advent of the early winter season, Circe was tutored in Illusions 
by Behemond.  Circe practiced her Illusions and her skill in Illusions went 
up.


  A fleet owing their allegiance to Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) 
invaded the province of the Starfish Sea, a Sea area owned by Circe.  
Bagmore (#75)'s forces took the Starfish Sea without any major engagements.  
Bagmore leads approximately 1 Eagles.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Circe for this year.


  Circe treated with her ally Bradipo I (#2).  Circe treated with her ally 
Lady of Beer Mbaba (#3).  Circe treated with her ally Hokuto (#4).  Circe 
treated with her ally Prometeo (#5).  Circe treated with her ally Kahn (#6). 
Circe treated with her ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Circe treated with her 
ally Agesilao (#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Attla (#54) fell into trouble with the law in Balmwood and escaped by 
riding away to Silvermist.
  Ashley (#74) heard stories of excellent fishing in Mare Imbrium and left 
Balmwood to take a vacation there.
  The 42nd Axemen has arrived in Katanga, having come from Chaco in search 
of employment.


  Here is the financial report for Circe's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 18 gold in revenue.  20 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Circe was left with 23 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Behemond
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  Hope (#94) encountered me.  Chanting her silver words of magic 
into a mighty Hand Of Death spell, Hope gestured with her hands and began 
making squeezing motions with her hands.  I stuck my tail between my legs 
and fled from Hope as fast as my legs could carry me!
  I moved into Siouxhome.  In my travels, I encountered no marauding 
monster.
  The wet spring was followed by a sultry early summer.  Hope encountered me.
Chanting her artful words of magic into a mighty Hand Of Death spell, Hope 
waved her hands and began making squeezing motions with her hands.  I stuck 
my tail between my legs and fled from Hope as fast as my legs could carry me!
  I moved into Rosehaven.  I encountered no marauding monster.
  In late summer, Hope encountered me.  Gesturing with her arms, Hope 
orchestrated otherworldly forces of magic, casting a Hand Of Death spell and 
began making squeezing motions with her hands.  Realizing that discretion is 
sometimes the better part of valor, I fled from the scene.
  I moved into the Io Sea.  I saw no monsters.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into fall.  I journeyed to Trouthome.  
I encountered no monsters.
  In early winter, I worked on my Illusions but was frustrated in my 
self-improvement efforts.
  Talking to some friendly farmers, I heard a rumor about a Hollow Tree in 
the Near-Beer Sea (#907), inhabited by the Elemental Sorceror.  They say 
that the Elemental Sorceror owns the Libram of Illusions.

  Thy humble servant,   Behemond


From: Gridley, Squire to Duqaq
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season Duqaq set out to quench his thirst 
for glory.  Thrym (#59) attempted a Kill Enemy spell, but botched it.  Duqaq 
moved into the Fourth Sea.  During his travels this season, Duqaq was 
spotted by a local patrol.  Their commanding officer threateningly 
challenged Duqaq.  He stuck his tail between his legs and fled from 
the Officer as fast as his legs could carry Duqaq!

  The wet spring was followed by early summer.  Thrym encountered Duqaq.  
Thrym chanted his strange words of magic and cast a Hand Of Death spell and 
began making squeezing motions with his hands.  Duqaq fled unceremoniously 
from the dangerous scene.
  Duqaq practiced his White Magic well, and even consulted a palm reader, 
but could not improve his White Magic.
  In late summer, Thrym encountered Duqaq.  Weaving his artful words of 
magic into a mighty Hand Of Death spell, Thrym waved his hands and began 
making squeezing motions with his hands.  Realizing that discretion is often 
the better part of valor, Duqaq fled unceremoniously from the dangerous 
scene.
  Duqaq practiced his White Magic well, and even consulted a palm reader, 
but could not improve his White Magic.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into the fall.  Thrym encountered Duqaq.  
Lifting his hands high in the air, Thrym cast a Hand Of Death spell and 
began making squeezing motions with his hands.  Duqaq turned around so as to 
flee from Thrym, but saw that his retreat route had been magically blocked 
by a curtain of fire.
  Duqaq cautiously advanced to bow range.  Thrym's unseen fingers pierced 
the forehead of Duqaq and dug into his brain and inflicted 3 damage points 
on Duqaq.  Thrym grabbed his spine with phantasmal hands and shook it 
ruthlessly and inflicted 3 damage points.
  Duqaq closed to melee range, filled with blood-lust.  Duqaq whirled about 
and audaciously swang at Thrym and missed by a mile.  His unseen fingers 
pierced the eyes of Duqaq and dug into his brain and walloped Duqaq with 3 
damage points.  Duqaq thrust at Thrym and would have struck him if Thrym 
hadn't sidestepped.  Thrym wrapped his phantasmal hand around Duqaq's heart 
and squeezed it viciously and damaged Duqaq, scoring 3 damage points.  Duqaq 
was mortally wounded.  And so it came to pass that Duqaq met his tragic end. 
Thrym relieved Duqaq of his treasure.  Thrym looted 1 gold from the treasure 
of Duqaq.

  Thy humble servant,   Gridley, Squire to Duqaq


From: Helatia
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter melted into spring.  I roamed around in Kerry, exploring the 
terrain there, and now 100% of it has been explored.  In my travels, I saw 
no wandering monster.
  During early summer, I moved into Khalturin.  I saw no marauding monsters.
  With the advent of the late summer season I rode into Katmai.  I saw no 
monster.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into fall.  I travelled about Katmai, 
exploring its features.  After my exploration efforts, 51% of it has been 
explored to date.  I also discovered a Glade (#26) in Katmai, occupied by 
the Treant.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  The Treant is a large 
tree capable of moving its limbs and arms much as a man does.  I was 
informed by some peasants of a feature in Katmai, a Great Hall (#106) where 
dwells the Renegade Illusionist.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  
The mysterious Renegade Illusionist is said to be a shadowy figure who uses 
his powers of deception to preserve his solitary existence.  In my travels, 
I encountered no marauding monsters.
  The fall darkened into the stillness of early winter.  I explored Katmai 
well and now 66% of it has been explored.  I found also that Katmai has been 
the site of terrible battles.  Brave and intrepid soldiers have given their 
lives on its fields: the 4th Bowmen (Veteran Elves) and the 5th Bowmen 
(Veteran Elves).  My experience raised my skill in Exploring.  While 
adventuring, I saw no monsters.
  I heard a rumor telling of a feature in Mongu (#305), a Cave where dwells 
the Renegade Swordsman.  The Cave is reputed to contain the Axe of the 
Dwarven Lords.

  Thy humble servant,   Helatia


From: Jamielle
To: Circe

