From: Frodo, Squire to Gabriel
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Arnulf (#19) encountered Gabriel.  Chanting his syllables of 
magic with trained precision, Arnulf let go a Hand Of Death spell and began 
making squeezing motions with his hands.  Gabriel ran shamelessly and fled 
from the combat.
  Gabriel journeyed in search of Bagmore (#75).  Gabriel caught up with 
Bagmore in the Iceberg Sea.  Gabriel looked for Bagmore in the Iceberg Sea.  
Gabriel could not encounter Bagmore because Bagmore led an army and Gabriel 
didn't.  His efforts raised his skill in Spying.
  During early summer, Arnulf (#19) encountered Gabriel.  Raising his hands 
high in the air, Arnulf cast a Hand Of Death spell and began making 
squeezing motions with his hands.  Gabriel fled from the dangerous scene.
  Gabriel journeyed in search of Bagmore (#75).  Gabriel rode into the 
Albatross Sea.  He caught up with Bagmore in the Albatross Sea.  Gabriel 
searched throughout the Albatross Sea for some sign of Bagmore.  Gabriel 
could not encounter Bagmore because Bagmore led an army and Gabriel didn't.  
During his travels, he was stopped by a local patrol.  Their commanding 
officer threateningly challenged Gabriel.  He ran furiously and fled from 
the encounter.

  Midsummer's day passed and a pleasant late summer came.  Arnulf (#19) 
encountered Gabriel.  Casting a Hand Of Death spell, Arnulf directed 
glowing, writhing strands of magic and began making squeezing motions with 
his hands.  Gabriel stuck his tail between his legs and fled from Arnulf as 
fast as his legs could carry Gabriel!
  Gabriel journeyed in search of Arnulf.  Gabriel caught up with Arnulf in 
the Albatross Sea.  Gabriel searched throughout the Albatross Sea for some 
sign of Arnulf.  Gabriel encountered Arnulf.  Gabriel raised his arms and 
gestured rhythmically, intending to cast a Mirror-Image Phantasm spell, but 
it went awry and a rabbit tumbled out of his sleeve instead.  Arnulf ran 
shamelessly and fled from the encounter.
  With the advent of the fall season, Arnulf encountered Gabriel.  Gesturing 
with his hands, Arnulf orchestrated otherworldly forces of magic, casting a 
Hand Of Death spell and began making squeezing motions with his hands.  
Deciding that discretion is sometimes the better part of valor, Gabriel fled 
unceremoniously from the dangerous combat.
  Gabriel travelled in search of Arnulf.  Gabriel caught up with Arnulf in 
the Albatross Sea.  Gabriel searched all throughout the Albatross Sea for 
Arnulf.  Gabriel encountered Arnulf.  Gabriel incanted his strange words of 
magic and cast a Mirror-Image Phantasm spell and an image of Arnulf sprang 
into existence!  Arnulf declined to enter personal combat.
  With the coming of the early winter season, Arnulf encountered Gabriel.  
Waving his hands, Arnulf juxtaposed otherworldly forces of magic, casting a 
Hand Of Death spell and began making squeezing motions with his hands.  
Gabriel tried to flee from the fight, but Arnulf cornered Gabriel.
  Gabriel loped along smoothly, conserving his energy, and closed to bow 
range.  Arnulf clenched his fist, squeezing the intestines of Gabriel and 
scored on Gabriel, doing 3 points of damage.  Arnulf curled his phantasmal 
hand around Gabriel's liver and squeezed it mercilessly and damaged Gabriel, 
scoring 3 damage points.
  Gabriel closed to melee range, seething with blood-lust.  Gabriel summoned 
all his strength and bravely thrust at his nemesis and missed badly.  The 
unseen hands of Arnulf grabbed his throat, choking Gabriel and walloped him 
with 3 damage points.  Gabriel moved closer and swang at Arnulf and missed 
by a mile.  Arnulf seized his neck with phantasmal hands and shook it 
violently and inflicted 3 damage points.  Gabriel staggered, stunned by the 
force of the mortal blow.  And so it was that Gabriel met his tragic end.  
Arnulf stooped to recover the personal belongings of Gabriel.  Arnulf found 1
gold in the hoard of Gabriel.

  Thy humble servant,   Frodo, Squire to Gabriel


From: Gunga Din, Squire to Alexius
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Alexius cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory armies were 
formed for Alexius.
  Jamielle's attempted cast of the Phantasmal Armies spell was unsuccessful.
  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Babba Sissoko (#0)ian empire 
marched on the Mountain province of Big Sky, a land garrisoned by the 
soldiers of Circe.  Tlazolteotl (#88) was in command of the invading armies. 
The defending forces were led by Alexius.  The armies were drawn up into 
lines of battle as shown here:

