  DEFENDING ARMY

  Tlazolteotl led her armies into the battle.  Standing tall with his 
warriors was Alexius.
  The army of Circe used magic to aid their cause.  Magical phantasmal 
armies fought with hers soldiers.  Tlazolteotl strode forward and challenged 
Alexius to personal combat.  Alexius declined to enter combat.
  The forces commanded by Alexius were dismayed by his faint-heartedness.  
They steadfastly marched on, though with lessened confidence.  The luck of 
Tlazolteotl's forces was good for this momentous occasion, for her men were 
in good spirits from a recent successful plundering expedition, and 
Tlazolteotl thus had a significant edge.  Also, she deployed her troops 
against Alexius with great tactical foresight and enjoyed a tremendous 
tactical advantage.

  On the right flank, the Veteran 139th Phalanx faced the 178th Garrison.  
The 256th Dragons swooped down on the 179th Garrison and attacked them.  The 
106th Dragons swooped down on the 178th Garrison and attacked without mercy. 
The 139th Phalanx battled with the 178th Garrison and overpowered them with 
their thundering charge.
  Out on the left wing, the Crack 222nd Phalanx were arrayed against the 
66th Garrison.  The 75th Dragons soared over the 66th Garrison and attacked 
them.  The 37th Elephants acquitted themselves most satisfactorily in 
battle.  The 222nd Phalanx battled the 66th Garrison and squashed them like 
rotten oranges.
  Tlazolteotl's great horde overwhelmed the army of Circe and took the 
field, scattering their enemies.  The 139th Phalanx destroyed the 178th 
Garrison.  The 222nd Phalanx scattered the 66th Garrison in all directions.  
The 256th Dragons slew the 179th Garrison almost to a man.  The 75th Dragons 
chased after the enemy and demolished the 37th Elephants.
  Tlazolteotl's campaign accomplished the conquest of Big Sky.  His forces 
completely destroyed, Alexius escaped frightened and alone to Kaluga.
  With the advent of the early summer season Alexius could find no soldiers 
in Kaluga for the requested Axemen troops.  So, Alexius tried to practice 
his Sageness, but the task was beyond his natural aptitude.  He invented 
nothing in his sagely researches.
  Midsummer's day passed and a hot late summer arrived.  Alexius cast a 
Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory armies were formed for Alexius.
  Alexius heard mention of an interesting feature in the Near-Beer Sea 
(#907): a Glade inhabited by the Centaur, who holds the Huge Hoard of Gold.
  During fall, Alexius attempted an illegal move.  He was already in Kaluga 
and could make no sense of the order to move to Kaluga.  So, Alexius 
discovered nothing in his sagely researches.
  With the coming of the early winter season, Alexius travelled to Khalturin.

  Thy humble servant,   Gunga Din, Squire to Alexius


From: Geoffrey
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I worked on my Meleeing but was thwarted in my self-improvement 
efforts.
  The wet spring was followed by early summer.  I rehearsed and practiced my 
Meleeing and improved noticeably.
  With the advent of the late summer season I practiced my Meleeing well, 
and even consulted a palm reader, but could not improve my Meleeing.
  While speaking with passing adventurers, I learned a rumor about a 
heretofore unknown Tomb in Katmai (#108), inhabited by the Bone Devil, who 
according to legend possesses the Needles of the Black Mage.
  During fall, I practiced my Meleeing for months, but could make no 
headway.
  The fall cooled into early winter.  I gathered my courage and my wits and 
entered the Hollow Tree.  I encountered the Medusa.  Incanting a Telekinetic 
Storm spell, I directed scintillating, writhing strands of magic and scored 
10 damage points on the Medusa.  The Medusa fell, mortally injured.  I 
turned my attention to the hoard of the Medusa.  I walked over to a pile of 
treasure and secured the Large Hoard of Gold.  I found a treasure of 22 gold 
and snarfed it up.
  I saw nothing special while scouting out the Hollow Tree.  In my travels, 
I encountered no monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Geoffrey


From: Jolin
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In late summer, I failed in my ineffectual attempt to cast a Plague spell.
  While speaking with adventurers, I learned a rumor about a heretofore 
unheard of Sacred Rock in Jerbilia (#605), inhabited by the Giant Eagle, who 
according to legend possesses the Large Hoard of Gold.
  The summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  I journeyed to Transylvania.  I 
